# NoiseModelling Benchmark

Compares several NoiseModelling versions on the same datasets (Clisson and La Montagne, France) and publishes the results as a
static website on GitHub Pages: <https://universite-gustave-eiffel.github.io/NoiseModellingBenchmark/>

## Where is what

| Path | What it does |
|---|---|
| `versions.json` | the list of versions to compare: `version -> release zip URL`. An **empty URL** marks the "head" version, taken from the NoiseModelling CI binary |
| `config/benchmark.json` | **single source of truth**: datasets, Java mapping, silence threshold, histogram bins, per-version simulation parameters and the V6 reference models |
| `benchmark_run_clisson.sh` | Clisson entry point — thin wrapper around `scripts/bench.sh --dataset clisson` |
| `benchmark_run_montagne.sh` | La Montagne entry point — thin wrapper around `scripts/bench.sh --dataset montagne` |
| `scripts/bench.sh` | the actual orchestration (download, run, aggregate), parameterised by `--dataset` |
| `scripts/lib/common.sh` | shared bash helpers: versions, download, binary discovery |
| `scripts/ci/` | CI helpers (`nm_versions.py`, `github_artifacts.py`) kept out of the workflow YAML |
| `bench/config.py` | loads `config/benchmark.json` |
| `bench/stats.py` | shared receiver parsing, LAEQ marking and silence threshold |
| `bench/compare.py` | unified comparison logic for both datasets |
| `compare_versions.py` | builds the Clisson pairwise comparisons (`comparisons.json`) — thin entry point over `bench/compare.py` |
| `compare_versions_montagne.py` | builds the La Montagne comparisons — thin entry point over `bench/compare.py` |
| `generate_site.py` | builds `website/index.html` from `website/template.html`, `config/benchmark.json` and the JSON files |
| `website/template.html` | the page structure (HTML only) |
| `website/js/` | the page JavaScript, split into ordered modules: `00-config`, `01-theme`, `02-helpers`, `03-cards`, `04-header`, `05-map`, `06-comparisons`, `07-histogram`, `08-boxplot`, `09-scatter`, `10-density`, `11-diffmap`, `12-montagne`, `13-montagne-map`, `14-start`, `15-sidebar`, `16-boot`. `js/00-constants.js` (histogram bins, silence threshold) is generated from `config/benchmark.json` |
| `website/index.css` | all the page CSS (dark and light themes in one file) |
| `website/data/` | **generated, not in git**: `results.json`, `comparisons.json`, `settings.json`, `build.json`, `start.json`, and one folder of map layers per version |
| `nm_version/src/main/groovy/` | the simulation scripts launched by NoiseModelling: `runscriptV5.0.groovy`, `runscriptV6.0.groovy`, plus one script per version when the API changed |
| `nm_version/src/main/groovy/lib/NoiseBench.groovy` | shared simulation helpers: script loading, profiler CSV, LAEQ statistics |
| `input/clisson/` | the Clisson reference dataset (Git LFS) |
| `input/montagne/` | the La Montagne dataset (Git LFS) and its measured reference `measure/RECEIVERS_LEVEL.geojson` |
| `schemas/` | JSON schemas of the generated artifacts, checked by `tools/validate_outputs.py` |
| `tools/` | the characterization harness: `run_checks.sh`, `snapshot.py`, `check.py`, `sim_spec.py`, `check_groovy.py`, `test_noisebench.py` |
| `docs/contracts.md` | the frozen compatibility contract (what must never change) |
| `.github/workflows/benchmark.yml` | the CI: one job matrix per Java version, the "head" job, the website build, the Pages deploy |
| `LICENSE` | GPL-3.0 |

## How it works

1. `benchmark_run_clisson.sh --version v5.0.1` downloads that release, then NoiseModelling's ScriptRunner runs
   `nm_version/src/main/groovy/runscriptV5.0.groovy` on `input/clisson/`; results land in `output/v5.0.1/`.
   The script to load and its parameters come from `config/benchmark.json`, not from hard-coded branches.
2. `benchmark_run_clisson.sh --aggregate-only` turns `output/*/` into `website/data/` and computes the comparisons.
3. `benchmark_run_montagne.sh --version v5.0.1` runs `nm_version/src/main/groovy/montagne/montagneV5.groovy` on
   `input/montagne/`; results land in `output/montagne/v5.0.1/`, and `--aggregate-only` builds
   `website/data/montagne/` (including the comparison to the measured levels).
4. The CI does 1–3 for every version of `versions.json`, then publishes `website/` on GitHub Pages.

Both entry points are thin wrappers; the orchestration lives in `scripts/bench.sh`.

## Run it locally

```bash
bash benchmark_run_clisson.sh --version v5.0.1   # one Clisson version
bash benchmark_run_clisson.sh                    # every version of versions.json (skips the head)
bash benchmark_run_clisson.sh --aggregate-only   # only rebuild the Clisson site data from output/
bash benchmark_run_montagne.sh --version v5.0.1  # one La Montagne version
bash benchmark_run_montagne.sh --aggregate-only  # only rebuild the La Montagne site data from output/montagne/
```

Needs Python 3, git-lfs (for `input/clisson/`) and Java 11 for v4/v5 or Java 25 for v6.
The NoiseModelling binary is downloaded automatically from the release URL in `versions.json`.

## Tests and guardrails

A refactor is only safe if the observable outputs stay identical. `tools/run_checks.sh` runs every
guard and must stay green:

| Tool | What it locks |
|---|---|
| `tools/check.py` | the pipeline and site outputs (normalised hashes) against `tools/baseline/snapshot.json` |
| `tools/sim_spec.py` | the simulation contract (script + parameters per version) against `tools/baseline/simulation_spec.json` |
| `tools/check_groovy.py` | every Groovy script still parses |
| `tools/test_noisebench.py` | the shared `lib/NoiseBench.groovy` helpers |
| `tools/check_js.py` | every website JS module parses (`node --check`) |
| `tools/render_check.py` | the rendered pages (Chrome headless) match `tools/baseline/render.json` |
| `tools/validate_outputs.py` | the generated artifacts match `schemas/` |

```bash
bash tools/run_checks.sh          # regenerate outputs and check everything
bash tools/run_checks.sh --no-run # check the current state without regenerating
```

When a change is intentional, accept the new baseline explicitly:

```bash
python3 tools/snapshot.py --update    # outputs
python3 tools/sim_spec.py --update    # simulation contract
```

The list of things that must never change is in `docs/contracts.md`.

## Rules that keep the results comparable

- A version runs with **Java 25** when its name starts with `v6`, with **Java 11** otherwise.
- Levels ≤ **-89 dB** are treated as `NaN`: excluded from means, histograms and comparisons (they appear as a
  `NaN` column in the histogram).
- The unreleased "head" version can be either an entry **without URL** in `versions.json` (built from a
  NoiseModelling CI artifact; on a fork this needs the optional `GH_PAT` secret and depends on a non-expired
  artifact being found) or an entry pinned to a **Maven Central snapshot URL** (built deterministically by the
  normal matrix). `v6.0.2-SNAPSHOT` is pinned this way; a new unreleased version is auto-added without URL by the CI.
- Do not modify `input/clisson/`: published results would no longer be comparable.
- For La Montagne, the comparison to the measurements is **calibrated per version**: `offset = measured − computed`
  at the receiver closest to the source (`input/montagne/LW_ROADS.geojson`), so the error is zero there for every model.
- Do not modify `input/montagne/` nor `input/montagne/measure/`: published results would no longer be comparable.
